const acceptance={status:'Partial diagnostic. l21 remains the owner-accepted base.',promoted:false,visualLaneMatchPassed:false,ownerAcceptedBase:21,awaitingOwnerReview:true,barColorPassed:errors.every(v=>Math.abs(v)<=.02),barColorErrorPercent:errors.map(v=>v*100),laneColorCloser:brownError(cLane)<brownError(oldLane),photoLaneToClearBrownColorRatio:pLane.brownColorRatio,l21LaneToClearBrownColorRatio:oldLane.brownColorRatio,l24LaneToClearBrownColorRatio:cLane.brownColorRatio,rmsIsGate:false,visualAssessment:'Native-column dust is now allowed to obscure and redden the bar. The new structure must still be judged against the connected, broad brown-orange lanes in the photo; numerical averages alone are not acceptance. The lanes are still too dark and fragmented, although their red-to-blue contrast improves. The final sheet and all three side views were inspected.',physicalAssumptions:'A 300 pc near-side offset for bar dust, a 250 pc centre-height dispersion with adopted 100 pc spatial correlation, and compact cloud depth equal to the 56 arcsecond transverse sample width. These are geometry priors, not measured individual cloud distances.',globalBudget:'The HERITAGE column is first multiplied everywhere by the single Bell overlap factor. The allowed global dust strength is then applied. At strength 2 the total covered column is twice the Bell-normalized baseline; no local column has its own scale.'};
