await writeFile(L24+'notes.md',`l24 is a partial diagnostic, changing only dust from the accepted l21. The connected brown lanes still do not match the photo, so l21 remains the base. Stellar density, point fluxes and colors, catalogue objects, component amplitudes and the display curve are unchanged.\n\nThe full HERITAGE columns replace the old five-arcminute high-pass modulation. Bell supplies one area-weighted normalization, ${num(normalization.factor).toFixed(4)}, over 85,397 shared native samples. No cell is normalized to a local Bell median.\n\nThe optical conversion is A_V = 7.394 Sigma_d mag, with Sigma_d in solar masses per square parsec, from Bell et al. 2022 equation 1 following Draine et al. 2014. This is a model-dependent conversion. The selected global dust strength is ${strength}, within 0.25–2. It is at the upper bound and makes the covered total ${strength.toFixed(2)} times the Bell-normalized baseline. Dense columns are neither clipped nor flattened.\n\nDense bar dust uses an adopted near-side offset of up to 300 pc. Positive disc height faces Earth. The 250 pc cloud-centre dispersion remains, with a fixed 100 pc spatial correlation so adjacent native cells have related depths. Each compact cell is about 13.5 pc wide and equally deep. Individual distances and this correlation are assumptions.\n\n| Masked bar close-up | R/G | B/G |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n${row('Horálek',color.photo)}\n${row('l21',color.l21)}\n${row('l24',color.l24)}\n\nThe relative bar color errors are ${errors.map(v=>(100*v).toFixed(2)+'%').join(' and ')}. The fixed HERITAGE lane-to-clear R/B ratios are ${num(pLane.brownColorRatio).toFixed(4)} for the photo, ${num(oldLane.brownColorRatio).toFixed(4)} for l21 and ${num(cLane.brownColorRatio).toFixed(4)} for l24. Missing HERITAGE support is excluded from these masks.\n\nTraining and held-out RMS are ${num(m.trainRelativeRms).toFixed(6)} and ${num(m.heldoutRelativeRms).toFixed(6)}, compared with 0.257606 and 0.309402 for l21. RMS did not decide the result.\n\nThe side views retain finite, coherent structure. Lane color and connected texture still fall short of the photo. The model lanes are too dark and fragmented; the higher global strength also makes some bar areas too dim. The owner should judge the close-up rather than the mean color alone. No full-resolution fitting or slab baking ran.\n`);
await writeFile(L24+'method.md',`The dust surface-density input is the [Gordon et al. 2014 HERITAGE BEMBB expectation map](https://doi.org/10.1088/0004-637X/797/2/85), unconstrained beta, from the [19 April 2014 author release](https://karllark.github.io/data_magclouds_dustmaps.html). Its 56 arcsecond samples are nominally independent. The [2017 erratum](https://doi.org/10.3847/1538-4357/aa6042) corrects quoted emissivities, while explicitly leaving the released mass maps and conclusions unaffected. This model uses the released columns directly, without refitting emissivity.\n\n[Bell et al. 2022, equation 1](https://doi.org/10.1093/mnras/stac1545), gives A_V = 0.7394 [Sigma_d / (10^5 solar masses per square kiloparsec)] mag, following Draine et al. 2014. In the released units this is A_V = 7.394 Sigma_d. Optical depth is A_V divided by 1.085736. The Gordon LMC extinction ratios already used by l21 remain unchanged. The MW foreground is kept separately.\n\nOne solid-angle-weighted ratio matches the integrated columns across the full common Bell/HERITAGE footprint. It is ${num(normalization.factor).toFixed(6)}. There is no normalization by individual Bell cells and no division by a blurred HERITAGE image. The allowed final dust strength multiplies this field globally; its value of ${strength} and the resulting deviation from the Bell baseline are reported explicitly. The unity-strength map contains 1,733 cells with A_V at least one magnitude, with a maximum near 22.5 mag.\n\nEach released sample becomes a compact positive 3D interpolation kernel. Its sky and line-of-sight widths are equal, so the surface map is not extruded into columns. The model reproduces the projected source column to well below one percent. Missing HERITAGE cells retain the l21 diffuse column, without adding another molecular budget.\n\nCloud centres follow the same warped disc. Their adopted Gaussian height scale remains 250 pc. A fixed 100 pc correlation keeps neighbouring depths related. A smooth, published bar-ellipse footprint receives a near-side offset of up to 300 pc; it becomes fully active by a calibrated A_V of 0.2 mag. This foreground ordering is an adopted hypothesis for the dust lanes, not an individual distance measurement. Its strength, depth realization and correlation are not fitted per pixel or region. All emitters and RGB grades remain frozen.\n\nThree trials are preserved. Independent cell depths and a 600 pc offset produced punctures. Correlated depths and a smaller offset reduced them. The last trial changed only global dust strength to its allowed upper bound. The final close-up, native column diagnostic and side views show both progress and remaining mismatch. No fourth correction was attempted.\n`);
